---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="CalcBadger's privacy policy: what we collect, what we don't, and how ads work.">
	<div class="mx-auto max-w-[680px]">
		<h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Privacy Policy</h1>
		<p class="mt-2 text-sm text-[var(--ink)]/50">Last updated: September 12, 2026</p>

		<div class="mt-6 text-[0.95rem] leading-[1.85] text-[var(--ink)]/75">
			<h2 class="font-display mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Calculator inputs</h2>
			<p class="mb-4">
				Numbers you type into any calculator on this site are processed entirely in your browser by
				client-side JavaScript. They are never transmitted to our servers, logged, or stored. There
				are no user accounts.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-display mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Hosting</h2>
			<p class="mb-4">
				The site is served by Cloudflare Pages, which processes standard technical request data
				(IP address, user agent) to deliver pages and protect against abuse, per
				<a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-display mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Analytics</h2>
			<p class="mb-4">
				We use Google Analytics 4 and Microsoft Clarity to understand how the site is used (pages
				viewed, time on page, approximate location, device type, and anonymized interaction
				recordings). Neither tool is used to identify you personally. See
				<a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">Google's privacy policy</a> and
				<a href="https://privacy.microsoft.com/privacystatement" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">Microsoft's privacy statement</a>.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-display mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Cookies and Advertising</h2>
			<p class="mb-4">
				Ad networks place cookies in your browser to serve ads (including ads personalized to your
				interests based on browsing activity), limit how often you see the same ad, measure ad
				campaigns, and detect fraud. Most browsers let you block or delete cookies in their settings;
				blocking cookies may still allow ads to display, just without personalization. You can also
				opt out of interest-based advertising at
				<a href="https://www.aboutads.info/choices" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">aboutads.info/choices</a> or, in the EU,
				<a href="https://www.youronlinechoices.eu/" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">youronlinechoices.eu</a>.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-display mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Third-Party Advertising Partners</h2>
			<p class="mb-4">
				<strong>Google AdSense.</strong> Google and its partners may use cookies and similar
				technologies to serve ads based on your visits to this and other sites. You can review how
				Google uses data at
				<a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites</a>
				and manage ad personalization at
				<a href="https://adssettings.google.com" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">adssettings.google.com</a>.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4">
				<strong>Adsterra.</strong> We also display ads served by Adsterra (Adsterra Ltd). Adsterra and
				its demand partners may set cookies or use similar identifiers to serve and measure ads,
				including interest-based ads; the data they process is described in the
				<a href="https://adsterra.com/privacy-policy/" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">Adsterra privacy policy</a>.
			</p>
			<p class="mb-4">
				Visitors in the EEA, UK, and Switzerland are shown a consent dialog before any advertising
				cookies are set. As the site grows we may add other advertising partners; any partner we add
				will have its own privacy policy and we will update this page to reflect it.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-display mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Your Rights</h2>
			<p class="mb-4">
				Depending on where you live (for example the EU/UK under GDPR, or California under CCPA/CPRA),
				you may have the right to access, correct, delete, or restrict the processing of personal data,
				and to opt out of the sale or sharing of personal information for targeted advertising. Because
				this site holds no accounts and no submitted data, most requests are satisfied by the cookie and
				ad-personalization controls above; for anything else, use the contact address below.
			</p>

			<h2 class="font-display mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Children's Privacy</h2>
			<p class="mb-4">
				This site is not directed at children under 13 and we do not knowingly collect personal
				information from them.
			</p>

<h2 class="font-display mt-6 mb-2 text-lg font-bold text-[var(--ink)]">Contact</h2>
			<p class="mb-4">
				Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:contact@calcbadger.com" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">contact@calcbadger.com</a> (see the <a href="/about/" class="text-[var(--flag-dark)] underline underline-offset-2">About page</a>).
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Layout>
